      <section>
        <h1>Voice Data Set Builder</h1>
        <p>My Voice data set builder project was built out of a personal frustration during my time at team hart when 
            my team and I struggled with finding vocal data sets to train a custom machine learning model for voice emotion
            recognition for the team Hart CUE project. I came up with an idea when watching the TV show Seinfeld where I found 
            that the actors often exaggerated the desired underlying emotions in order to make it extremely clear to audiences,
            furthermore since scripts outline emotions explicitly before lines so the actors know how to say the line, this can 
            be used to create annotated data sets by matching the lines in the script to the audio using simple speech to text and 
            then simply interpreting the actor's annotations around the line to be the tag for the vocal audio frame. 
        </p>

